ke</surname><given-names>GS</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Looking into the institutional review board: observations from both sides of the table</article-title><source>J Nutr</source><year>2005</year><volume>135</volume><fpage>921</fpage><lpage>4</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15795462</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b9-co13_2p055"><label>9</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group><name><surname>Slater</surname><given-names>EE</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>irb reform</article-title><source>N Engl J Med</source><year>2002</year><volume>346</volume><fpage>1402</fpage><lpage>4</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11986417</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b10-co13_2p055"><label>10</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group><name><surname>Bernstein</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Fully informed consent is impossible in surgical clinical trials</article-title><source>Can J Surg</source><year>2005</year><volume>48</volume><fpage>271</fpage><lpage>2</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16149359</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b11-co13_2p055"><label>11</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group><name><surname>Joffe</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Cook</surname><given-names>EF</given-names></name><name><surname>Cleary</surname><given-names>PD</given-names></name><name><surname>Clark</surname><given-names>JW</given-names></name><name><surname>Weeks</surname><given-names>JC</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Quality of informed consent in cancer clinical trials: a cross-sectional survey</article-title><source>Lancet</source><year>2001</year><volume>358</volume><fpage>1772</fpage><lpage>7</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11734235</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b12-co13_2p055"><label>12</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group><name><surname>Etchells</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name></perso